          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To find the 11th term from the last term, we will find the total number of terms in the AP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.184,
            0.135,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.183,
            0.652,
            0.203
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "- 6 2 = 1 0 + ( n - 1 ) ( - 3 )"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.418,
            0.208,
            0.605,
            0.227
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "- \\; 7 2 = ( n - 1 ) ( - 3 )"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.234,
            0.523,
            0.253
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e., n – 1 = 24"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.259,
            0.523,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "or n = 25"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.284,
            0.472,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, there are 25 terms in the given AP."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.309,
            0.901,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The 11th term from the last term will be the 15th term. (Note that it will not be the 14th term. Why?)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.354,
            0.135,
            0.372
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.354,
            0.71,
            0.375
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "a_{15} = 10 + (15 - 1)(-3) = 10 - 42 = -32"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.379,
            0.522,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e., the 11th term from the last term is – 32."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.404,
            0.333,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Alternative Solution :"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.429,
            0.895,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we write the given AP in the reverse order, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = - 6 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and d = 3 (Why?) So, the question now becomes finding the 11th term with these a and d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.481,
            0.134,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.311,
            0.479,
            0.746,
            0.501
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "a_{11} = -62 + (11 - 1) \\times 3 = -62 + 30 = -32"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.505,
            0.654,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the 11th term, which is now the required term, is – 32."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.537,
            0.902,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 9 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A sum of ` 1000 is invested at 8% simple interest per year. Calculate the interest at the end of each year. Do these interests form an AP? If so, find the interest at the end of 30 years making use of this fact."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.601,
            0.822,
            0.621
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We know that the formula to calculate simple interest is given by"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.355,
            0.633,
            0.629,
            0.675
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{SimpleInters} = \\frac{\\mathrm{P} \\times \\mathrm{R} \\times \\mathrm{T}}{100}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.68,
            0.724,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the interest at the end of the 1st "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "year =\\frac{\\frac{1000 \\times 8 \\times 1}{100}}{\\frac{100}{100}}=\\frac{\\frac{2}{5}80}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.727,
            0.733,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The interest at the end of the 2nd "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "year =\\frac{1000\\times8\\times2}{100}=\\xi160"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.772,
            0.733,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The interest at the end of the 3rd "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "year =\\frac{\\frac{1000 \\times 8 \\times 3}{100}}{100}=\\frac{\\frac{\\pi}{4}240}{\\frac{1000 \\times 8 \\times 3}{100}}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}240"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.821,
            0.878,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, we can obtain the interest at the end of the 4th year, 5th year, and so on. So, the interest (in `) at the end of the 1st, 2nd, 3rd, . . . years, respectively are"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.877,
            0.581,
            0.897
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_11_equation_25.jpg",
          "content": "8 0 , 1 6 0 , 2 4 0 , \\ldots"
        },
